{"text": "CONFIDENTIAL SETTLEMENT COMMUNICATION -- SUBJECT TO FRE 408 AND LOCAL RULE 83.6\n\n                    MEDIATED SETTLEMENT TERM SHEET\n\nMatter:    Achterberg v. Tidewater Cold Storage, LLC, et al.\nCourt:     U.S. District Court, Eastern District of Virginia (Norfolk Division)\nCase No.:  2:25-cv-00417-RBS-LRL\nMediator:  Hon. Lucille Baptiste-Moreau (Ret.), Harborview Dispute Resolution Group\nDate:      October 9, 2026\n\n1. PARTIES. Plaintiff Rosalind M. Achterberg (\"Plaintiff\" or \"Ms. Achterberg\").\nDefendants Tidewater Cold Storage, LLC (\"Tidewater\") and its managing member,\nDesmond Okonkwo-Hale (\"Okonkwo-Hale\").\n\n2. PAYMENT. Tidewater will pay a gross sum of $185,000.00\n(one hundred eighty-five thousand dollars), allocated as follows:\n   (a) $52,400.00 as back overtime wages, less withholding, reported on Form W-2;\n   (b) $52,400.00 as liquidated damages, reported on Form 1099-MISC (box 3);\n   (c) $6,200 in settlement of the accommodation claim (EEOC Charge No.\n       437-2025-01186) arising from her high-risk pregnancy;\n   (d) $74,000.00 in fees and costs to Pruitt & Vandermeer, PLLC (EIN 54-1830927).\n\n3. TIMING AND DELIVERY. Payments (a)-(c) within 21 days of court approval and in no\nevent later than November 20, 2026. Checks to Plaintiff go to\n2217 Colley Avenue, Apt. 3B, Norfolk, VA 23517. For the W-2, payroll will use the SSN on file\nending xxx-xx-0681; Plaintiff gives her W-9 to counsel only.\nPayment (d) by wire to the firm's IOLTA account: Chesapeake Tidal Bank, ABA 052476475,\nacct 0004 1882 7731, reference PV-25-0417.\n\n4. INSURANCE. Tidewater's EPLI carrier, Old Dominion Mutual Casualty Co. (\"ODMC\"),\nclaim no. EPL-2025-0093317 under policy ODM-EPL-7704512, funds $110K of the gross\nsum. Tidewater funds the $75,000 balance from its retention. Adjuster with authority:\nKwame Asante, (757) 555-0163 x214, kasante@odmc-claims.example.\n\n5. NON-MONETARY TERMS. Neutral reference limited to dates of employment (06/03/2019\nto 01/17/2025) and last position held. Separation re-coded as voluntary; no\ncontest of unemployment benefits. Mutual non-disparagement. No rehire.\n\n6. RELEASE. General release of wage claims under 29 U.S.C. § 216(b) and state law.\nCarve-out: her pending workers' compensation claim (JCN VA02000394417) for\na lumbar disc herniation is NOT released.\n\n7. APPROVAL. Joint motion for approval to be filed by 10/23/2026. Counsel:\nTamsin Pruitt (VSB No. 48213) for Plaintiff; J. Everett Lindqvist III,\nLindqvist Shaw & Abernathy LLP, for Defendants.\n\nInitialed:  RMA ____   DOH ____   TP ____   JEL ____\n\nMediator's note: Judge Baptiste-Moreau holds the signed sheet. Rosalind asked\nthat nothing be mailed to the Ghent apartment after Dec. 1, when her lease ends;\nuse r.achterberg77@mailbox.example or her cell, 757.555.0128, after that.", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "391 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Rosalind M. Achterberg", "Desmond Okonkwo-Hale", "Kwame Asante", "Tamsin Pruitt", "J. Everett Lindqvist III", "Judge Baptiste-Moreau", "Rosalind"], "companies": ["Tidewater Cold Storage, LLC", "Harborview Dispute Resolution Group", "Pruitt & Vandermeer, PLLC", "Old Dominion Mutual Casualty Co.", "Lindqvist Shaw & Abernathy LLP", "example"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.2000000011175871, "modelMs": 25691.5, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "passport_dl", "routing", "phone", "record", "vin", "account", "money", "dob", "age90", "date", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "names"], "detections": [{"start": 144, "end": 154, "text": "Achterberg", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Rosalind M. Achterberg"}, {"start": 158, "end": 185, "text": "Tidewater Cold Storage, LLC", "kind": "company", "source": "model", "canonical": "Tidewater Cold Storage, LLC"}, {"start": 285, "end": 306, "text": "2:25-cv-00417-RBS-LRL", "kind": "record", "source": "pattern", "canonic